errors is module
errors purpose "Show raising, catching, recovering from, converting, and passing up errors"
errors path errors
errors imports standard.console
errors imports standard.string
errors imports standard.compare
errors exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

showInt is operation
showInt purpose "Print one whole number on its own line"
showInt invariant none
showInt typeParameter none
showInt input value Int64 copied
showInt output none
showInt outputOwnedBy none
showInt raises none
showInt effect write console.stdout
showInt uses stdoutWriter
showInt memoryHeap false
showInt async false
showInt maxRecursion none
showInt label begin loopKind none
showInt label begin within none
showInt label done loopKind none
showInt label done within none
showInt let none
showInt at begin do writeValue
showInt at begin branch ifError writeValue goto done else goto done
showInt at done return ok none

writeValue is call
writeValue rationale "A test program has nowhere to report a failed write"
writeValue in showInt
writeValue invokes console.writeIntegerLine
writeValue argument value Int64 value copy
writeValue result none
writeValue ownedBy none
writeValue cleanedBy none
writeValue borrows none
writeValue catch writeError console.WriteError
writeValue suppresses console.WriteError.failed

ConfigError is enum
ConfigError purpose "Why a configuration value was rejected, with the detail needed to report it"
ConfigError typeParameter none
ConfigError variant notANumber none
ConfigError variant tooLarge Int64

parsePort is operation
parsePort purpose "Parse a port number, converting the library's parse error into a ConfigError"
parsePort invariant none
parsePort typeParameter none
parsePort input text String borrowed
parsePort output Int64
parsePort outputOwnedBy none
parsePort raises ConfigError
parsePort effect none
parsePort uses none
parsePort memoryHeap false
parsePort async false
parsePort maxRecursion none
parsePort label begin loopKind none
parsePort label begin within none
parsePort label badText loopKind none
parsePort label badText within none
parsePort label checkRange loopKind none
parsePort label checkRange within none
parsePort label rejectLarge loopKind none
parsePort label rejectLarge within none
parsePort label accepted loopKind none
parsePort label accepted within none
parsePort let largest Int64 65535 immutable
parsePort at begin do parse
parsePort at begin branch ifError parse goto badText else goto checkRange
parsePort at badText do makeNotANumber
parsePort at badText return error notNumber
parsePort at checkRange do tooBig
parsePort at checkRange branch if isTooBig goto rejectLarge else goto accepted
parsePort at rejectLarge do makeTooLarge
parsePort at rejectLarge return error tooLargeError
parsePort at accepted return ok port

parse is call
parse in parsePort
parse invokes string.toInt64
parse argument text String text lend
parse result port Int64
parse ownedBy none
parse cleanedBy none
parse borrows none
parse catch parseError string.ParseError
parse suppresses none

makeNotANumber is call
makeNotANumber in parsePort
makeNotANumber invokes ConfigError.notANumber
makeNotANumber argument none
makeNotANumber result notNumber ConfigError
makeNotANumber ownedBy none
makeNotANumber cleanedBy none
makeNotANumber borrows none
makeNotANumber catch none
makeNotANumber suppresses none

tooBig is call
tooBig in parsePort
tooBig invokes compare.greaterThanInt64
tooBig argument left Int64 port copy
tooBig argument right Int64 largest copy
tooBig result isTooBig Bool
tooBig ownedBy none
tooBig cleanedBy none
tooBig borrows none
tooBig catch none
tooBig suppresses none

makeTooLarge is call
makeTooLarge in parsePort
makeTooLarge invokes ConfigError.tooLarge
makeTooLarge argument payload Int64 port copy
makeTooLarge result tooLargeError ConfigError
makeTooLarge ownedBy none
makeTooLarge cleanedBy none
makeTooLarge borrows none
makeTooLarge catch none
makeTooLarge suppresses none

loadPort is operation
loadPort purpose "Parse a port, passing any ConfigError up unchanged"
loadPort invariant none
loadPort typeParameter none
loadPort input text String borrowed
loadPort output Int64
loadPort outputOwnedBy none
loadPort raises ConfigError
loadPort effect none
loadPort uses none
loadPort memoryHeap false
loadPort async false
loadPort maxRecursion none
loadPort label begin loopKind none
loadPort label begin within none
loadPort label passUp loopKind none
loadPort label passUp within none
loadPort label done loopKind none
loadPort label done within none
loadPort let none
loadPort at begin do parseIt
loadPort at begin branch ifError parseIt goto passUp else goto done
loadPort at passUp return error innerError
loadPort at done return ok parsed

parseIt is call
parseIt in loadPort
parseIt invokes parsePort
parseIt argument text String text lend
parseIt result parsed Int64
parseIt ownedBy none
parseIt cleanedBy none
parseIt borrows none
parseIt catch innerError ConfigError
parseIt suppresses none

portOrDefault is operation
portOrDefault purpose "Parse a port, recovering with port 0 when the text is not a number"
portOrDefault invariant none
portOrDefault typeParameter none
portOrDefault input text String borrowed
portOrDefault output Int64
portOrDefault outputOwnedBy none
portOrDefault raises none
portOrDefault effect none
portOrDefault uses none
portOrDefault memoryHeap false
portOrDefault async false
portOrDefault maxRecursion none
portOrDefault label begin loopKind none
portOrDefault label begin within none
portOrDefault label recover loopKind none
portOrDefault label recover within none
portOrDefault label done loopKind none
portOrDefault label done within none
portOrDefault let fallback Int64 0 immutable
portOrDefault at begin do tryParse
portOrDefault at begin branch ifError tryParse goto recover else goto done
portOrDefault at recover return ok fallback
portOrDefault at done return ok parsed

tryParse is call
tryParse rationale "Recovering with a default is this operation's purpose"
tryParse in portOrDefault
tryParse invokes parsePort
tryParse argument text String text lend
tryParse result parsed Int64
tryParse ownedBy none
tryParse cleanedBy none
tryParse borrows none
tryParse catch ignoredError ConfigError
tryParse suppresses none

main is operation
main purpose "Run the case and print what it computes"
main invariant none
main typeParameter none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwnedBy none
main raises none
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memoryHeap false
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main label showGood loopKind none
main label showGood within none
main label inspect loopKind none
main label inspect within none
main label showRejected loopKind none
main label showRejected within none
main label broken loopKind none
main label broken within none
main let goodText String "42" immutable
main let wordText String "port" immutable
main let largeText String "70000" immutable
main let two Int64 2 immutable
main let three Int64 3 immutable
main let rejectedCode ExitCode 3 immutable
main let failCode ExitCode 1 immutable
main let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable
main at begin do loadGood
main at begin branch ifError loadGood goto broken else goto showGood
main at showGood do printGood
main at showGood do loadDefault
main at showGood do printDefault
main at showGood do loadLarge
main at showGood branch ifError loadLarge goto inspect else goto broken
main at inspect match largeError ConfigError
main at inspect case ConfigError.notANumber bind none none goto broken
main at inspect case ConfigError.tooLarge bind rejected Int64 goto showRejected
main at showRejected do printTwo
main at showRejected do printThree
main at showRejected return ok rejectedCode
main at broken return ok failCode

loadGood is call
loadGood in main
loadGood invokes loadPort
loadGood argument text String goodText lend
loadGood result goodPort Int64
loadGood ownedBy none
loadGood cleanedBy none
loadGood borrows none
loadGood catch goodError ConfigError
loadGood suppresses none

